------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The GPU hardware video paths (NVIDIA NVENC/NVDEC, AMD AMF, Intel QSV/oneVPL)
are implemented as **hand-rolled FFI in this repository** (under
crates/codec/src/{encode,decode}/), declared against the respective vendor SDK
headers (NVIDIA Video Codec SDK, AMD AMF SDK, Intel oneVPL) and loading the
vendor runtime libraries dynamically at runtime via dlopen. The underlying
vendor SDKs are proprietary and are not redistributed with this software. No
third-party GPU wrapper crates are used.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Opus encoder and decoder (crates/opus, the rivet-opus repository,
https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-opus, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author, written from
RFC 6716 as updated by RFC 8251, and RFC 7845. They do not include or derive
from libopus, FFmpeg or any other Opus implementation: none was read, copied
or translated. Where RFC 6716 makes its attached reference code normative,
that code was used as specification only, described in prose by one author
and implemented from the description by another. The official Opus test
vectors are used as data only. Opus is covered by patents whose holders have
made royalty-free licensing commitments to the IETF.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MPEG audio decoder (Layers I, II and III) and MP3 encoder (crates/mp3, the
rivet-mp3 repository, https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-mp3, under the
same licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same
author, written from ISO/IEC 11172-3 and 13818-3, the public descriptions of
the MPEG-2.5 extension and of the Xing, LAME and VBRI tags, and published
psychoacoustic literature. They do not include or derive from minimp3, LAME,
mpg123, libmad, FFmpeg or any other MPEG audio implementation, none of which
was read or run; the normative tables are the standards' data. The decoder
is verified against ISO's conformance waveforms, used as data. The principal
MP3 patents are generally regarded as expired.

