The FLAC and ALAC (Apple Lossless) audio decoders and encoders (crates/lossless,
the rivet-lossless repository, https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-lossless,
under the same licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original
implementations by the same author, written for this project from the FLAC
format specification (IETF RFC 9639), the published Apple Lossless format
description, and published literature on linear prediction and Rice coding.
They contain no code from libFLAC, FFmpeg, Apple's ALAC reference
implementation or any other codec implementation. The Apple Lossless format
was published by Apple Inc. under the Apache License, Version 2.0; FLAC is an
open, royalty-free format.

For each of these codecs, as for AAC, this software grants no patent rights
and makes no claim about whether a licence is needed.

